    {
      "id": "claim_ddc886854d624dba801e53828331d114",
      "statement": "The evidence check reads git check-ignore's exit status precisely — 0 means ignored and fails, 1 means committable and passes, anything else is reported as an unchecked error — because treating any non-zero status as success once let a git failure report retained evidence as safe.",
